(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Background: Adjunctive therapies targeting both motor and cognitive domains may enhance) Tj
T*
(outcomes in schizophrenia beyond pharmacotherapy alone. Objective: To evaluate whether) Tj
T*
(combining Baduanjin practice with computerized cognitive remediation produces greater) Tj
T*
(benefits than cognitive training without movement intervention. Methods: A total of 120) Tj
T*
(hospitalized schizophrenia patients \(mean age 44 years; 67% male\) were randomized to) Tj
T*
(either combined therapy \(n=60\) or cognitive remediation only \(n=60\). Sessions occurred 5) Tj
T*
(days per week for 8 weeks. Outcome measures included PANSS \(psychiatric symptoms\), NCSE) Tj
T*
(\(cognition\), SSPI \(social functioning\), and SQLS \(quality of life\). Results: At 8 weeks,) Tj
T*
(the combined-treatment group showed greater reduction in PANSS total scores \(mean) Tj
T*
(reduction 14.2 points versus 8.7 points, P = 0.003\). Improvements in negative symptom) Tj
T*
(subscales were particularly pronounced \(P = 0.001\). Cognitive performance and social) Tj
T*
(functioning indices also favored the combined approach \(all P < 0.05\). No serious adverse) Tj
T*
(events occurred in either group. Conclusion: Addition of Baduanjin to cognitive) Tj
T*
(remediation significantly enhances therapeutic benefit for psychiatric symptoms and) Tj
T*
(functional domains in schizophrenia.) Tj
